### Spring Boot Redis + MySQL POC - HTTP Requests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. Actuator Health Check (MySQL + Redis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Actuator Caches (Inspect active Redis cache managers)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/caches
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create Product 1 (Mechanical Keyboard)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard",
  "category": "electronics",
  "price": 149.99,
  "stock": 50,
  "description": "Tenkeyless mechanical keyboard with Cherry MX switches"
}

### 4. Create Product 2 (Wireless Mouse)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wireless Mouse",
  "category": "electronics",
  "price": 79.99,
  "stock": 100,
  "description": "Ergonomic wireless mouse with 4000 DPI sensor"
}

### 5. Get Product by ID (1st call: Cache miss -> loads MySQL; 2nd call: Cache hit -> Redis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/products/1
Accept: application/json

### 6. Get Product View Count (Atomic Redis counter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/products/1/views
Accept: application/json

### 7. List All Products (Cached in Redis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/products
Accept: application/json

### 8. Search Products by Category (Cached in Redis)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/products/search?category=electronics
Accept: application/json

### 9. Update Product (Updates MySQL, updates single cache, evicts list/search caches)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical Keyboard RGB",
  "category": "electronics",
  "price": 169.99,
  "stock": 45,
  "description": "Updated with per-key RGB backlighting"
}

### 10. Delete Product (Deletes from MySQL, evicts all related caches)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/products/2

